    affiliation: "Post-Industrial School; Langara College"
abstract: >-
  Jason Roberts' 2010 formula for luck, L = D × T (luck equals doing times
  telling), treats telling as a quantity. This research argues that telling is
  also an environment. An exploratory survey of eight founders found that
  the environment where they spent the most time (social platforms, 9.4 hours
  a month) returned the least perceived serendipity (2.62 out of 5), while
  structured events took less than half the time and returned the most
  (3.62). The essay proposes a revised formula, L = D × T × e, and three tests
  for the environment term: constraint, frame and friction.
keywords:
